[NVIDIA] Simplify fixed-cluster program IDs (#11790)

`%clusterid.x` expands in `ptxas` into a general unsigned division of
the CTA ID by the runtime cluster width. One observed expansion contains
26 SASS instructions:

<details>
<summary>Before: expansion of <code>%clusterid.x</code></summary>

```sass
CS2R.32 R10, SR_CgaSize;
IMAD R10, R10, -0xa0, RZ;
R2UR UR8, R10;
LDCU UR8, c[0x0][UR8+0x2a0];
S2UR UR9, SR_CTAID.X;
I2FP.F32.U32 R10, UR8;
UIADD3 UR4, UPT, UPT, URZ, -UR8, URZ;
MUFU.RCP R8, R10;
I2FP.F32.U32.RZ R9, UR9;
VIADD R8, R8, 0xfffffffe;
FMUL.RZ R6, R8, R9;
F2I.U32.TRUNC.NTZ R6, R6;
R2UR UR6, R6;
UIMAD UR4, UR4, UR6, UR9;
I2FP.F32.U32.RZ R9, UR4;
UIADD3 UR4, UPT, UPT, URZ, -UR8, URZ;
FMUL.RZ R8, R8, R9;
F2I.U32.TRUNC.NTZ R8, R8;
R2UR UR5, R8;
UIADD3 UR5, UPT, UPT, UR6, UR5, URZ;
UIMAD UR4, UR4, UR5, UR9;
UISETP.GE.U32.AND UP0, UPT, UR4, UR8, UPT;
USEL UR4, URZ, 0xffffffff, !UP0;
UISETP.EQ.U32.AND UP0, UPT, UR8, URZ, UPT;
UIADD3 UR4, UPT, UPT, UR5, -UR4, URZ;
USEL UR25, UR4, 0xffffffff, !UP0;
```

</details>

For `num_ctas == 2`, the replacement is a CTA-ID read and a right shift:

```sass
S2UR UR7, SR_CTAID.X;
USHF.R.U32.HI UR25, URZ, 0x1, UR7;
```

