commits.message:
[NVIDIA] Use redux for 64-bit integer min/max reductions (#11788)

Lower full-warp 64-bit integer min/max reductions using two 32-bit
`redux.sync` operations. Reduce the high words with the original
signedness, then reduce the low words only from lanes whose high word
won.

Idea:
```cpp
high = uint32_t(x >> 32);
low  = uint32_t(x);

winningHigh = redux_max(high);  // Original signedness.
eligibleLow = high == winningHigh ? low : 0;
winningLow  = redux_umax(eligibleLow);

result = (uint64_t(winningHigh) << 32) | winningLow;
```

